  "body": "## What and why\n\nAdd Help > Tips and an optional tip on the start page for #3030.\n\n- Keep four tips in `assets/tips/tips.json`. UI and MCP read that file.\n- Add `list_tips` as a read-only tool. It does not change the document or undo history.\n- Resolve the undo shortcut for the screen's OS. The MCP server uses its own OS.\n- Keep the start tip below the normal actions. Hide it during generation, import, AI work and stock precalculation.\n- Persist Don't show again in the existing per-user preferences. Help > Tips remains available and can restore the start tip.\n- Open existing guide pages from Show me. Do not add new CAM actions or change output checks.\n\nThe undo tip distinguishes an attached agent from a headless document. The example tip does not promise a project for every operation.\n\n## Tests and readings\n\nBase: `1c0152c9106514622a641c17adc7520af45ebc6a`.\n\n- Base RED: `list_tips_is_listed_and_read_only` failed because the tool was absent. The Help structural test failed because Help was absent.\n- Sabotage RED: removing the new registry entry made the MCP pin fail again. Restoring it passed.\n- GREEN: shared ids, four tip contents, source/response equality, repository link targets and Windows/Linux/macOS shortcuts.\n- GREEN: Help window, shared text, guide action, named launcher refusal/recovery, screen OS shortcuts, nonblocking start tip, running generation suppression and persistent opt-out with synthetic preferences.\n- GREEN: existing Home layout and the new Tips window layout.\n- GREEN: selected quick gate, six steps: app lib, mcp, mcp_doc_drift, mcp_provider, view_prefs and ui lib.\n- GREEN: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --lib --test mcp --test mcp_provider --test mcp_doc_drift --test view_prefs -- -D warnings`.\n- GREEN: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`.\n- GREEN: focused site tests `test_release_027_batch3.py` and `test_ai_guide.py`.\n- All four tip URLs returned HTTP 200. Tests also check their repository targets.\n\nThe selected gate command was:\n\n```sh\nCAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3 CAMCRAFT_GATE_SWEEP=off cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main \\\n  --only 'app suites: lib' --only 'ui suites: lib' \\\n  --only 'app suites: mcp' --only 'app suites: mcp_provider' \\\n  --only 'app suites: mcp_doc_drift' --only 'app suites: view_prefs'\n```\n\n## Limits\n\nThe full quick plan selects 188 steps after MCP registration. The six directly affected steps above ran and passed. No post or toolpath changed.\n\nThe light dry-run selects 11 geometry twins and a full motion/app release build with `--no-run`. The assigned scope excludes that release rebuild for this UI-only change. The light lane was NOT RUN; it is not a reported pass. No full heavy, catalog or release gate ran.\n\nNative tips rotate by UTC day. Browser builds use the first start tip without a native clock call. The Help window lists all tips. No browser build or physical machine was tested. The optional site Tips page is not added; no second text store exists.\n\nEffort: medium\nChangelog: Add Help tips, a persistent start-page tip preference and the read-only list_tips MCP tool.\n\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3030#issuecomment-7203144792\n\nFixes #3030\n",
